FILE-03: write FILLTIME and DRAINTIME rule values in decimal hours

The rule parser reads a FILLTIME or DRAINTIME value as a decimal number
of hours, as the manual describes, but writepremise() wrote it as
h:mm:ss, like a clock time. getfloat() rejects "1:30:00", so a saved
file with such a rule failed to open with error 202. The writer now
writes these two values as decimal hours with four decimals.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-03_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/rules.c b/src/rules.c
index 1b009ad..f104fd8 100644
--- a/src/rules.c
+++ b/src/rules.c
@@ -1414,11 +1414,15 @@ void writepremise(Spremise *p, FILE *f, Network *net)
         switch (p->variable)
         {
         case r_CLOCKTIME:
-        case r_DRAINTIME:
-        case r_FILLTIME:
         case r_TIME:
             gettimetxt(p->value, s_value);
             break;
+
+        // Fill and drain times are read back as decimal hours
+        case r_DRAINTIME:
+        case r_FILLTIME:
+            sprintf(s_value, "%.4f", p->value / 3600.0);
+            break;
         default: sprintf(s_value, "%.4f", p->value);
         }
     }
